ng Tan\n\nSep 06 2023 math.CO arXiv:2309.00757v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2309.00757, author = {Imre Leader and Žarko Ran\\djelović and Ta Sheng Tan}, title = {{A} {N}ote on {H}amiltonian-{I}ntersecting {F}amilies of {G}raphs}, year = {2023}, eprint = {2309.00757}, note = {arXiv:2309.00757v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nHow many graphs on an $n$-point set can we find such that any two have connected intersection? Berger, Berkowitz, Devlin, Doppelt, Durham, Murthy and Vemuri showed that the maximum is exactly $1/2^{n-1}$ of all graphs. Our aim in this short note is to give a 'directed' version of this result; we show that a family of oriented graphs such that any two have strongly-connected intersection has size at most $1/3^n$ of all oriented graphs. We also show that a family of graphs such that any two have Hamiltonian intersection has size at most $1/2^n$ of all graphs, verifying a conjecture of the above authors.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nResearch (https://users.math.msu.edu/users/ovenhou3/research.html)\nciteturn4search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 8 months ago; ## Research Interests ... Arxiv:2306.14389\n(with Gregg Musiker, Ralf Schiffler, and Sylvester W. Zhang)\nto appear in Algebraic Combinatorics (2026)\nArxiv:2306.14389\n  * Eigenvalues of Matrix Products\n(with Richard Kenyon)\nBulletin of the London Mathematical Society (2025)\nArxiv:2407.10786\n  * Higher-Rank Dimer Models\n(with Richard Kenyon)\nTransactions of the American Mathematical Society (2025)\nArxiv:2312.03087\n  * Noncommutative Networks on a Cylinder\n(with Semeon Arthamonov and Michael Shapiro)\nCommunications in Mathematical Physics (2024)\nArxiv:2008.02889\n  * q-Rational and q-Real Binomial Coefficients\n(with John Machacek)\nAdvances in Applied Mathematics (2023)\nArxiv:2301.08185\n  * q-Rationals and Finite Schubert Varieties\nComptes Rendus Mathematique (2023)\n-----------------------------------